	"FriendlyName": "FireLane - Friendly Fire & Line-of-Fire Gate",
	"Description": "The check every AI shooter needs and almost none has: is one of my own people standing in the shot? A single line trace is not enough - a bullet has width, a team-mate walks, and the answer arrives one frame late. FireLane sweeps a lane of the projectile's real radius from muzzle to target, projects every friendly forward along its own velocity so the shot is judged against where people will be, and separates a hard block from a graze so the AI is neither reckless nor mute. When the lane is blocked it does not just say no: it returns the sideways step that would clear it, so the squad moves instead of standing there. Geometry checks run on a per-frame trace budget, so sixty shooters cost what you decide they cost.",
	"Category": "AI",
	"CreatedBy": "Silvan Teufel",
